Z||000011||recluse||11-20-2001||04:12 PM||||<BR>Just curious -- why do I have to remove the slave cylinder?[/B][/QUOTE]<P>You meant master, but you have to remove it to take the old push rod out and put the new one in.  Theres a washer around the push rod that is held into the master cylinder with a snap ring.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Phil||11-20-2001||04:53 PM||||Just a note, I have removed the push rod from the master without removing the master. It's a GREAT help if you have a pair on snap ring pliers. I removed the snap ring and pulled the push rod out. I did have a short wooden dowel handy to keep the plunger from coming out but it stayed in there on it's own. Fortunately my spine is made out of rubber and I could get under the dash.||||reg||1
